Package: zypper-declarative
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Declarative system convergence for zypper (Machinery subset)
 zypper-declarative converges a SUSE system to a desired manifest expressed in
 the declarable subset of the SUSE Machinery system description (packages,
 repositories, services, config_files). It applies inside a single snapshot
 transaction, records what was applied, and is idempotent. It also describes
 the actual state, computes diffs, and verifies drift.
